# Large live-run preflight

Never start a full or large live corpus run without first running a representative preflight on the same corpus, provider, profile, models, prompts, and candidate limits.

The preflight is not a two-case smoke test. It has two mandatory parts: (1) a full-corpus structural budget pass covering every query-dependent retrieval branch, and (2) a representative real-LLM pass exercising planner, reranker, final LLM, citations, fallback path where applicable, progress/checkpoint writing, and all budget counters. Before the full run, Astra must read both raw traces and record an explicit acceptance artifact.

The preflight must fail acceptance if any of these are unknown or wrong:

- the reranker receives the configured evidence limit (currently 20) for every applicable case;
- the upstream wide pool is an internal diagnostic only; it may be larger than 20, and an exact value of 80 is not a user-facing candidate contract;
- final evidence is at most 40 and downstream payload is at most 25;
- planner, reranker, and final LLM calls are observed, with the configured fallback chain recorded;
- stage metrics, citation metrics, warnings, errors, and latency are present;
- corpus/provider/profile/model/prompt hashes match the planned full run;
- the corpus gold schema contains the fields required by the declared metrics (`doc_id`, `point_number`, `point_identity_key`, `chunk_id`, and `answer_excerpt`) for every quality case; missing gold fields block acceptance rather than becoming silent zero metrics;
- the metric definition distinguishes strict point identity, chunk, document, answer span, and citation.

The structural pass must cover the entire planned corpus and show zero configured reranker-input shortfalls. A wide-pool value below the internal diagnostic target of 80 is recorded, but is not a gate failure when at least 20 items reach the reranker. A representative LLM pass cannot substitute for this full-corpus check, because retrieval budget failures below the contractual 20 are query-dependent.

Never silently replace a configured limit with a larger one to make the gate pass. If a preflight invariant fails, do not launch the full run. Fix the harness or record the run as invalid for comparison. After a full run, audit misses against the canonical document text before changing retrieval, reranking, parsing, prompts, or models.
